-- title:
--   Evaluated Point Family Self Consistency Of Strongly Self Consistent
-- statement:
--   **Strong self-consistency transfers to evaluated point measurements.**
--
--   Let `params` be the test parameters, `strategy` a symmetric projective strategy, and `family` an indexed polynomial submeasurement. If `family` is strongly self-consistent with error $\zeta$ under `hself`, then polynomial evaluation on the two tensor registers preserves the state-dependent squared-distance bound under uniform points:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{sddError}\left(\psi,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}),\operatorname{evaluatedPointFamilyLeft},\operatorname{evaluatedPointFamilyRight}\right)\le\zeta.
--   $$
--
--   The proof combines slice strong self-consistency with evaluation postprocessing and the uniform identification of the successor point space with the product of the base point space and the slice-height field.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedPointFamily_selfConsistency_of_stronglySelfConsistent`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
